{"name":"Rub Elbows","hex":"#5f5547","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rub elbows","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To associate closely; to consort, mingle, or socialize. .mw-parser-output .object-usage-tag{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output .deprecated{color:var(--wikt-palette-grey-lime-8,olivedrab)}[with with]"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rub_elbows"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elbow","blocks":[{"text":"The elbow is the region between the upper arm and the forearm that surrounds the elbow joint. The elbow includes prominent landmarks such as the olecranon, the cubital fossa, and the lateral and the medial epicondyles of the humerus. The elbow joint is a hinge joint between the arm and the forearm; more specifically between the humerus in the upper arm and the radius and ulna in the forearm which allows the forearm and hand to be moved towards and away from the body.\nThe term elbow is specifically used for humans and other primates, and in other vertebrates it is not used. In those cases, forelimb plus joint is used."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Elbow_on_gray_background.jpg/330px-Elbow_on_gray_background.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/LeftHumanPosteriorDistalHumerusExtended.jpg/500px-LeftHumanPosteriorDistalHumerusExtended.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/LeftHumanPosteriorDistalHumerusExtended.jpg/500px-LeftHumanPosteriorDistalHumerusExtended.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeftHumanPosteriorDistalHumerusExtended.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/MedialHumerusRadiusU